th d=3D"M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></pat=
h></svg></button></div></div></h1><p><a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.=
01332">arXiv:2203.01332</a><span>, has finally appeared in a journal, and <=
/span><strong>yes, it took us more than four years to get it to publication=
</strong><span data-state=3D"closed" style=3D"min-width: 0px;"><a data-comp=
onent-name=3D"FootnoteAnchorToDOM" id=3D"footnote-anchor-2" href=3D"https:/=
/superposer.substack.com/p/postquantum-gravity-new-results-and#footnote-2" =
target=3D"_self" class=3D"footnote-anchor">2</a></span><strong><span>. When=
 it comes to publishing and writing up results, we suffer from </span><a hr=
ef=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Distracted_boyfriend">distracted boyfri=
end syndrome</a><span>.</span></strong></p><p><span>The most general form o=
f Markovian (memoryless) quantum quantum dynamics is the Lindblad or GKSL e=
quation. The most general form of stochastic classical dynamics is the Fokk=
er-Planck equation for continuous dynamics, and the Kolmogorov=E2=80=93Fell=
er equation for discrete jumps. Examples of consistent classical-quantum dy=
namics were introduced in the mid-1990s by </span><a href=3D"https://arxiv.=
org/abs/hep-th/9409189">Blanchard and Jadczyk</a><span>, and by </span><a h=
ref=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/9503023">Di=C3=B3si</a><span>. In the=
 </span><a href=3D"https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/1sy3-dyb6"=
>General form of continuous hybrid classical-quantum dynamics</a><span>, we=
 proved the most general form of such dynamics. This is important because i=
t means that we can now prove general theorems about any theory in which sp=
acetime remains classical. And this is important for experiments.</span></p=
><p><strong>The only way to test whether spacetime has a quantum nature, is=
 to compare what quantum gravity predicts, with what the alternative hypoth=
esis would predict</strong><span>. An example of such a result is that any =
classical theory of spacetime must satisfy the </span><a href=3D"https://ww=
w.nature.com/articles/s41467-023-43348-2">decoherence-diffusion trade-off</=
a><span>, and this can be experimentally tested via two different experimen=
ts. A recent addition to the experimental landscape is the recent proposal =
by Fabiano</span><span>, </span><span>Fujita</span><span>, </span><span>Mat=
sumura</span><span>, </span><span>and Carney,  </span><a href=3D"https://ar=
xiv.org/abs/2603.26075">Minimal noise in non-quantized gravity</a><span>.</=
span></p><h2 class=3D"header-anchor-post">Emergence of phantom cold dark ma=
tter<div class=3D"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position=
-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent"><div class=3D"pencraft pc-display-=
contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div id=3D"=C2=A7emergence-of-phantom-co=
ld-dark-matter" class=3D"pencraft pc-reset header-anchor offset-top"></div>=
<button tabindex=3D"0" type=3D"button" aria-label=3D"Link" data-href=3D"htt=
